# playpick cell: mode=menus view=844x390,touch save=carried
#
# First mode=menus session at 844x390 landscape combined with a carried
# profile (the one prior 844x390 menus session, 2026-09-30-17-navigation.mjs,
# was 820x1180; the one prior carried-menus session at this exact size does
# not exist). #272 ("pick The Long Haul, leave, come back, selection reverts
# to RAID") was only ever reproduced via a full page `open` (reload) in
# playtest/plans/2026-09-25-7.play. That leaves an open question this session
# answers: does the in-app BACK button lose the pick the same way, or only a
# reload does -- which would narrow the bug from "not persisted to storage"
# to "not restored from live JS state on back-navigation" or vice versa.
#
# Also checks class-pick memory (README: "your pick is remembered between
# visits") through the same in-app back path rather than a reload, and runs
# `ui` at this squat 390px-tall shape on both the battleground setup and
# class-pick screens, which no prior session has measured at 844x390.

open
targets
shot frontpage
ui

# Pick a battleground map, then leave via in-app BACK (not reload/open).
tap battleground
targets
shot bgsetup-conquest
ui
tap map:escort
targets
state
shot bgsetup-escort-picked
ui

tap back
targets
state
shot after-back-from-bgsetup

# Re-enter battleground setup: is escort still selected in-app?
tap battleground
targets
state
shot bgsetup-reentered
ui

tap back

# Now the class-pick memory question, same in-app-back path.
tap raid
targets
shot raid-roster
ui
tap next
targets
shot class-select
ui
tap class:hunter:marksmanship
targets
state
shot class-picked
tap back
tap back
targets
state
shot after-back-from-class

tap raid
tap next
targets
shot class-select-reentered
ui
